# Patch:        020-raw-data-bounds
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       multi-stark/src/backend.rs, multi-stark/src/config.rs, multi-stark/src/contract/constraints.rs, multi-stark/src/contract/table.rs, multi-stark/src/rounds/repr.rs
# Hunks:        11
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 10 (charon#1266): baby-bear's pre 020
#               drops `Field`'s `RawDataSerializable` supertrait under the
#               cfg. Without this patch p3-multi-stark does not compile there:
#               E0277 and E0599, a field's bytes are not available, 4 times,
#               and 11 more once those are bounded.
# Cost:         none: each added bound is implied by `Field` in a normal
#               build.
# Upstreamable: no: the bounds are redundant upstream. Dropping baby-bear's
#               pre 020 makes them unnecessary.
# Drop when:    baby-bear's pre 020 is dropped.
# Test:         test p3-multi-stark --test mixed_width
# Mutation:     the configuration's trace field must also be an iterator,
#               which `TranscriptField` does not imply, so the test's
#               configuration no longer compiles.
#
# Two places read a field element's bytes:
#
# - the contract encodes the constraints of each table, scalar by scalar;
# - the representation backend indexes a lookup table by an element's first byte.
#
# Under the cfg `Field` no longer implies the serialization, so each bound on the way states it.
#
# The configuration trait states it on its trace and challenge fields, which covers the verifier's entry points.
#
# Every one of the 15 is needed: removing any one fails the cfg build.
#
# In a normal build `Field` implies each bound, so the upstream configurations still satisfy the trait.
#
